{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1461909-m20-ritual-questions","id":1461909,"title":"M20 Ritual Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-28T20:56:03-07:00","id":1461909,"title":"M20 Ritual Questions","content":"I'm going to be in an upcoming M20 game soon and I've been looking through the rulebook and haven't found anything that prevents ritual &quot;stacking&quot;. (Using multiple rituals to give the same effect) If that is the case, is it not possible for a Mage to be running around with excessively powerful effects? (As in game-breaking) <br /> <br /> Secondly, some Spheres (as far as I can tell) have the power to improve or lower your / enemies dice pools. (Looking at you Entropy) <br /> <br /> This coupled with ritual &quot;stacking&quot; being a possiblity means that a Mage who has spent enough time casting could be running around with 100+ dice to every roll. <br /> <br /> Is there any clause that would prevent this? As I can't find any so far. If so please share it. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26413-thatonekiasyd","name":"ThatOneKiasyd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26413_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T05:15:50-07:00","id":1461939,"title":"","content":"While I haven't found the rule in M20, it was the case in older editions that the mechanics of effects overlap, rather than stack.<br /> <br /> That is, If you cast a spell to increase your strength in 2 and another that would increase it in 3, you would have a +3 to Str, not a +5 (and the duration of each effect it's sepparate, so, if the +2 was a ritual with a long duration and the +3 was for a scene, after the end of the scene you would return to hav a +2).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T05:43:56-07:00","id":1461944,"title":"","content":"While an anti-stacking house rule is a good idea, there are existing rules that help mitigate things:<br /> <br /> 1) For every two effects you have running you get a +1 difficulty on your magic rolls (with some exceptions). Casting lots of self-buffs will have you at serious risk of botching a ritual long before you get dozens of spells going.<br /> <br /> 2) Pattern Bleed and Permanent Paradox are going to be issues, and make #1 even worse. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T05:46:25-07:00","id":1461946,"title":"","content":"I would love to hear others chime in on this.<br /> <br /> One thing about Mage: The Ascension. As a system, it requires a bit of cooperation between the players and the ST to work correctly. If a player decides they are going to break the game, exploit everything they can find to their advantage or be a rules lawyer... you're going to have a bad time. If you are really into tight game mechanics, maybe pick up Mage: The Awakening instead. Mage: The Ascension is more like jazz. Lots of improvisation, cooperation, give and take, that kind of thing.<br /> <br /> While this doesn't explicitly call out &quot;stacking&quot; per se...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> P. 537-538<br /> <br /> Picking Up Where You Left Off<br /> <br /> After casting an imperfect Effect or falling short of her initial plans, a mage can pick up where she left off by making another roll at +1 to the original difficulty. In story terms, she grits her teeth, regroups, and gives it the old (wizard) college try once again.<br /> <br /> For situations in which you try again due to a failed roll \u2013 or try again and fail the roll \u2013 check out the Failed Rolls entry below. In other cases, an extended roll might be in order\u2026 and for those situations, again see the Rituals, Rolls, and Extended Successes entry below. </div> </div> </div>So a Mage who creates an Effect to increase her Strength wants to do it again to increase her Strength even more, would probably fall under this rule, as her first attempt &quot;fell short&quot; of what she wanted.<br /> <br /> There are other limits as well.<br /> <br /> -Every time you fail an Arete roll on a ritual, your difficulty climbs by 1.<br /> <br /> -If you botch an Arete roll, you have to spend a willpower point and one of your successes to keep going, AND you get the increased difficulty. If you DON'T you botch the ritual and get a big paradox whammy equal to the number of rolls you have made -1.<br /> <br /> -If you have multiple effects on your character at once, they can increase difficulty if they require her concentration.<br /> <br /> -If it is a really long ritual, you may start to take penalties from exhaustion. You can do rituals for your stamina in hours before taking penalties. (There is an optional rule to determine how long an arete roll takes for a ritual; if you are shooting for 10+ successes, it is a &quot;great work&quot; and each roll takes 5 hours. Great works can be paused, but it takes willpower, and a skill check to get started again. That's an expensive pee break!)<br /> <br /> -You are only allowed a number of arete rolls based on your arete+willpower.<br /> <br /> All these penalties really add up, as Arete is a very small dice pool and it is easy to fail rolls or botch them.<br /> <br /> Also, any effect that is adding a large number of dice to a pool (one might say, superhuman,) is almost certainly going to cause paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1078,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","user":"Froggy711","date":".  error 10-02-2021, 12:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T10:01:28-07:00","id":1462437,"title":"","content":"I just realized a mistake I made in my previous post. Each roll for a &quot;great work&quot; ritual is 5 hours of time, not 1 hour. My apologies.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, offhandedly, I wanted to mention that one mistake I see a lot of newer players make is assuming that Arete is rolled <i>with </i>something when creating effects. Sometimes they add the highest sphere (this is something Mage: The Awakening does) or allows adding some relevant skill (see Skills Enhancing Magick on P.533 for how this can be done.) Arete is always rolled by itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T10:19:25-07:00","id":1462439,"title":"","content":"Note that skills enhancing magic doesn't actually add a skill to the magic roll. The skill gets rolled separately, and then it's successes get used to reduce the difficulty of the magic roll. There are no official ways to add anything else to the roll that I am aware of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T13:34:50-07:00","id":1462473,"title":"","content":"Mind 1 and Life 3 both allow you to increase your Attributes, which would then increase your dice-pools.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T18:57:37-07:00","id":1462504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1461909-m20-ritual-questions?p=1462473#post1462473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind 1 and Life 3 both allow you to increase your Attributes, which would then increase your dice-pools.</div> </div> </div> </div>But not to an Arete roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T22:57:16-07:00","id":1462516,"title":"","content":"Right.<br /> <br /> Though then you get the group casting rules which can expand your Arete rolls significantly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}